  "raw_text": "The session surfaced an occult_dependency in the tooling infrastructure: sys_adm is designated as the source of truth for shell scripts, ~/bin is the runtime deployment, but no mechanism enforces consistency between them. Scripts updated in sys_adm silently diverge from what runs until manually copied, a gap that materialized mid-session when desktop_backup was updated in sys_adm but ~/bin still held the old version. The commissive act \u2014 \"I am thinking an addon to sys_adm in wrapup or something similar, part of the major pivot is cleaning up\" \u2014 parks a planned resolution: a deploy step keyed to recent git changes in sys_adm, integrated into the /wrapup session-close sequence. The tribal_knowledge operating here is that deploy steps are not administrative overhead but the structural link between authorship and execution. The resonance state is friction_named rather than harmony_restored: the gap is identified, the fix is commissioned, and the session closes without implementing it \u2014 deferral acknowledged rather than forgotten.",
